WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.393 --> 00:00:03.366
- When we get pulled over in the Batcars,

00:00:03.366 --> 00:00:04.996
luckily a lot of the police officers

00:00:04.996 --> 00:00:06.838
just want their picture taken with it.

00:00:06.838 --> 00:00:07.844
Yes sir, you can.

00:00:07.844 --> 00:00:09.001
Please do.

00:00:09.001 --> 00:00:11.982
We created the Batcar for the
Michael Keaton Batman movie,

00:00:11.982 --> 00:00:14.021
the Mystery Machine from Scooby-Doo,

00:00:14.021 --> 00:00:15.829
everything from Herbie the Love Bug

00:00:15.829 --> 00:00:18.589
to the Landspeeder from Star Wars.

00:00:18.589 --> 00:00:21.659
We create a lot of wild
rides out of some junk.

00:00:21.659 --> 00:00:25.353
(lighthearted music)

00:00:25.353 --> 00:00:26.484
In the past two or three years,

00:00:26.484 --> 00:00:29.734
we've created 15, 16 iconic movie cars.

00:00:31.679 --> 00:00:35.125
I had a real job at one
time at a major airline.

00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:38.294
We initially started out
refurbishing old cars.

00:00:38.294 --> 00:00:40.759
We decided we were gonna
start making some iconic cars

00:00:40.759 --> 00:00:42.660
that you could actually
get in and out of it,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.817
drive it, kids can climb
on it and look at it.

00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:48.227
Typical builds can be anywhere from

00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:52.220
as little as two weeks,
to as much as three years.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.902
The Speed Racer Mach 5
sitting here beside us

00:00:54.902 --> 00:00:56.810
started off as a 94 Corvette.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.697
Hopefully here in about 30
days it'll be finished up,

00:00:58.697 --> 00:01:00.871
have a great big honking
M on the hood of it,

00:01:00.871 --> 00:01:02.256
and it'll look awesome.

00:01:02.256 --> 00:01:04.402
There's a tremendous
amount of trial and error.

00:01:04.402 --> 00:01:07.640
A lot of these cars have a
lot of fiberglass on 'em.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.081
It's a labor of love to come out

00:01:09.081 --> 00:01:10.403
and just continue putting down

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.346
layers and layers of fiberglass.

00:01:12.346 --> 00:01:15.285
You can't go to O'Riley's
or Advanced Auto Parts

00:01:15.285 --> 00:01:18.036
and ask 'em for a part for a Batcar.

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:18.869
(upbeat music)

00:01:18.869 --> 00:01:21.085
Our Eleanor from Gone in
60 Seconds car up front

00:01:21.085 --> 00:01:23.872
is absolutely as screen-
accurate as we can get it.

00:01:23.872 --> 00:01:27.436
From the stainless aluminum
interior to the seats

00:01:27.436 --> 00:01:29.980
to the shifter, the go
baby switch in the center.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.153
And we drive Eleanor just like
it's supposed to be driven.

00:01:32.153 --> 00:01:33.396
That's why it was built.

00:01:33.396 --> 00:01:34.905
(engine revving)

00:01:34.905 --> 00:01:37.822
(tires screeching)

00:01:40.189 --> 00:01:42.251
Everything we have we take out and drive.

00:01:42.251 --> 00:01:43.499
Every single piece.

00:01:43.499 --> 00:01:46.816
We take it all to the local
stores, we'll go to McDonald's.

00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:50.983
What better thing to get
groceries in than the Batcar?

